{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["Benjamin, a wolf, tears prey — concerning Saul, who was the first king, it was prophesied that he ravaged all the surrounding nations, as it is written there: ״בכל אשר יפנה ירשיע״ — that he wreaked havoc upon all the nations. And also Benjamin was with the righteous kings of Judah who prevailed over the nations, as written concerning Asa, Jehoshaphat, and Hezekiah." "And at evening he divides spoil — for such is the habit of a wolf: ״זאב ערבות ישדדם״, ״כזאבי עקב לא גרמו לבקר״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:53.220109039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}